// codebox_real.gen -- f_wave_field stage 6: the real-space stage on the inverse-DFT result.
// 256x256 float32. Mirror: tests/modules/wave_field/wave_field_mirror.real_stage().
//
// Inputs: first = the inverse DFT (R = u, B = v), second = the force texture (cold; the module's inlet 0 through
// vs_inState: WHERE), third = last frame's state from the hold stage (cold), fourth = the LFO texture (cold; the
// module's inlet 1 through its own vs_inState: WHEN). Output = the new solver state and the feedback edge:
//   R = u, G = pin flag (1 on a frame the pin applied), B = v, A = 1 (A held the exciter phase until the exciter was
//   removed, 2026-11-04, D7)
//   - connected flags (from vs_inState, via `prepend param`): src_force (inlet 0) and src_lfo (inlet 1). An unconnected
//     inlet is vs_black = 0, which would decode to a full -1 force, so every read is gated on its flag. The gates use
//     switch(), not multiplication, so a NaN in the unused branch cannot leak (0 * NaN). The flags lag ~180 ms at load
//   - T (the LFO time function, T035) = the LFO's R channel per pixel, raw 0..1 (lmode 0, uni) or 2 x - 1 (lmode 1, bi,
//     mid-grey neutral), and 1 when no LFO is connected. A uniform and a spatial LFO both work
//   - force (FR-007): v += force * 2 (tex - 0.5) * T * dt, only with inlet 0 connected (mid-grey does nothing). With
//     nothing on inlet 0 there is no push, whatever the LFO does. A uniform force only feeds the DC bin, which the spec
//     stage removes
//   - strike (FR-009; D11 / D12, T042): a held PRESS, not an impulse. While strike_gate is 1 (and reset_gate is 0) u is
//     PINNED toward target = strength * amp * T with weight pw: u += pw (target - u), and v is killed where pinned,
//     v *= 1 - pw. pw and amp are the OUTLINE mask of inlet 0 and 1 (OUTLINE_AMP) when it is connected, else the
//     gaussian at the frame centre (0.5, 0.5; sigma 0.02, wrapped distance) and 4 (STRIKE_AMP). The pin REPLACES u at
//     the pinned texels (a press on a ringing field does not add there; Matt, 2026-11-04) and is idempotent, so the old
//     counter and the G memory are gone: a tap is a gate the patcher holds for a few draws. No gain constant: the
//     amplitude is in field units. The outline mask is |I(x+1) - I(x-1), I(y+1) - I(y-1)| of the R channel of inlet 0,
//     one solver texel either side, the neighbour's texel index clamped to 0..255 and read at its texel centre (never
//     at a coordinate on or past the seam: out-of-range reads wrap, and nearest() there is unmeasured,
//     tests/lib/gpu_sim.py; this equals the mirror's edge padding), result clamped to 0..1. Read with nearest() at the
//     inlet's own resolution, so an inlet smaller than 256 gives a band about two solver texels wide at each of ITS
//     texel boundaries (checked live in T034, not in the mirror). While reset_gate is on the pin waits. Param named
//     strike_gate, not gate: `gate` is a Gen operator name (the same clash as `edge`). The hold texture is still read
//     (in3) so the inlet count and wiring stay put; its G is no longer used
//   - sponge (FR-010): exp(-rate dt) on u and v, rate = edge_amt * 20 (SPONGE_RATE) * smoothstep profile over the
//     border band of width 0.12 (SPONGE_WIDTH). edge 0 leaves the periodic wrap
//   - containment: non-finite / huge values zapped to 0 (abs(x) < 1e30), then clamped to +-100 (U_CAP)
//   - Param names: never a one-letter name (`t` was silently never applied); `edge_amt` (`edge` is
//     a Gen operator name; the dial and the message keep the plain word `edge`)
Param dt(0.016666667);
Param force(1);
Param strength(1);
Param lmode(0);
Param src_force(0);
Param src_lfo(0);
Param edge_amt(0);
Param strike_gate(0);
Param reset_gate(0);

dx = norm.x - 0.5;
dy = norm.y - 0.5;
dx = dx - floor(dx + 0.5);
dy = dy - floor(dy + 0.5);
prof = exp(0 - (dx * dx + dy * dy) / 0.0008);

holdg = nearest(in3, norm).y;
holdg = switch(abs(holdg) < 1e30, holdg, 0);

uu = nearest(in1, norm).x;
vv = nearest(in1, norm).z;

conn = switch(src_force > 0.5, 1, 0);
lraw = nearest(in4, norm).x;
tt = switch(src_lfo > 0.5, mix(lraw, lraw * 2 - 1, lmode), 1);

ff = switch(conn > 0.5, force * 2 * (nearest(in2, norm).x - 0.5) * tt, 0);
vv = vv + ff * dt;

cxi = floor(norm.x * 256);
cyi = floor(norm.y * 256);
xr = (min(cxi + 1, 255) + 0.5) / 256;
xl = (max(cxi - 1, 0) + 0.5) / 256;
yu = (min(cyi + 1, 255) + 0.5) / 256;
yd = (max(cyi - 1, 0) + 0.5) / 256;
gx = nearest(in2, vec(xr, norm.y)).x - nearest(in2, vec(xl, norm.y)).x;
gy = nearest(in2, vec(norm.x, yu)).x - nearest(in2, vec(norm.x, yd)).x;
omask = clamp(sqrt(gx * gx + gy * gy), 0, 1);

pinon = switch(strike_gate > 0.5, 1, 0) * switch(reset_gate < 0.5, 1, 0);
pw = pinon * switch(conn > 0.5, omask, prof);
ptarget = strength * switch(conn > 0.5, 1, 4) * tt;
uu = uu + pw * (ptarget - uu);
vv = vv * (1 - pw);

edist = min(min(norm.x, 1 - norm.x), min(norm.y, 1 - norm.y));
sp = clamp(1 - edist / 0.12, 0, 1);
sprate = edge_amt * 20 * sp * sp * (3 - 2 * sp);
gs = exp(0 - sprate * dt);
uu = uu * gs;
vv = vv * gs;

uu = switch(abs(uu) < 1e30, uu, 0);
vv = switch(abs(vv) < 1e30, vv, 0);
uu = clamp(uu, -100, 100);
vv = clamp(vv, -100, 100);

out1 = vec(uu, pinon + 0 * holdg, vv, 1);
